{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>When he sends forth — אֶת בְּעִירָהּ וּבִעֵר.</b> All are a term for beast, as in ״אֲנַחְנוּ וּבְעִירֵנוּ״ (Numbers 20)." "<b>When he sends forth.</b> He leads his animals into the field or vineyard of his fellow, and damages it in one of these two ways — either by sending forth his beast or by grazing — and our Sages explained: ״וְשִׁלַּח״ is damage by the settling of the foot; ״וּבִעֵר״ is damage by the tooth, that eats and grazes (Bava Kama 2)." "<b>In another's field.</b> In the field of another man." "<b>The best of his field … he shall pay.</b> We assess the damage, and if he comes to pay him land for the money of his damage, he pays him from the best of his fields — if his damage was a sela, he gives him the value of a sela from the best quality he has. Scripture teaches you that damages are assessed at best-quality land (Mekhilta; Bava Kama 6)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:50.472857631Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}